            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बदतमीज़ — badtamīz — \"rude; ill-mannered\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "वह लड़का बहुत बदतमीज़ है, बड़ों का आदर नहीं करता। vah laṛkā bahut badtamīz hai, baṛoṁ kā ādar nahīṃ kartā. That boy is very rude; he doesn't respect his elders."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बदतमीज़ (badtamīz) is usually traced to Persian bad, \"bad\", joined to Arabic tamīz, \"discernment, good manners\", which came through Persian: having bad manners."
            }
          ]
        },
